{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli and ruled as Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Pons Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III's reign was marked by the rise of Saladin's power in the region.\n\n* **Early Life and Reign*** \nRaymond III was the son of Pons Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father Pons died in 1152 when Raymond was just a child and he succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. He was just 3 years old when he became the ruler of Tripoli. During his early years as Count of Tripoli he was under the regency of his mother Hodierna.\n\n* **Reign and Military Campaigns*** \nAs Raymond III grew older he took control of the government of Tripoli from his mother. He was known for his bravery and military skills. Raymond III played a significant role in the Second Crusade and was one of the leaders of the Crusader forces. He also participated in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 where he led the Crusader forces to victory.\n\nRaymond III was a skilled diplomat and was able to secure the support of the Crusader states for his rule. He was also known for his tolerance towards the Muslim population of Tripoli and was able to maintain good relations with them.\n\n* **Death and Legacy*** \nRaymond III died in 1187 after being captured by Saladin's forces. He was imprisoned in Damascus and later executed. His death marked the end of the House of Tripoli and the County of Tripoli was eventually absorbed into the Ayyubid Empire. Raymond III's legacy is remembered as a brave and skilled military leader who played a significant role in the history of the Crusades.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of",